2. Correction subsystem  —  adapted from IHCONCS_2026_paper (MIT)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Files: kazmorph/correction/*.py
  - correction_metrics.py
  - keyboards.py
  - corrupt.py
  - freq.py
  - candidate_generator.py
  - corrector_3way.py
  - __init__.py

The three-way KEEP/CORRECT/REVIEW corrector, the four-mode candidate generator
(with stem recombination), the nine-operator controlled-error generator, the
correction-quality metrics (FCR, CER, WER, Recall@K, MRR, risk–coverage), and
the leakage-free corpus frequency dictionary were adapted from the
IHCONCS_2026_paper project (MIT License).

These modules are MIT-licensed as part of kazmorph. Adaptations were limited
to import-path fixes and replacing the source project's ``config`` module with
module-level constants; the decision logic and metrics are functionally
unchanged.


3. Cross-validation and significance testing  —  adapted from CAGF-CBT-CRF (MIT)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files:
  - kazmorph/cv.py            (leakage-free k-fold CV: stratified + grouped)
  - kazmorph/significance.py  (Wilcoxon, Cohen's d, Holm-Bonferroni, bootstrap CI)

The fold-construction logic (LPT block scheduling, jack-knife invariants,
self-contained deterministic PRNG) and the paired significance-testing
functions were adapted from the CAGF-CBT-CRF project (MIT License).

These modules are MIT-licensed as part of kazmorph. For cv.py the adaptation
was reading ``sent_id`` from kazmorph's Sentence attribute instead of CoNLL-U
comment lines; for significance.py the CLI was dropped and scipy is now
imported lazily so the pure functions work without it.


